body:
@ldv-alt What do you think of searching for the last slash from the end instead of using `dirname()` and `basename()`.
I was initially fearing that this would require handling escaping, but it seems on Linux at least that it's not possible to have a slash in the file name at all.
It may be on Windows (+ NFS or Samba), but in such case there won't be SELinux labels for sure, so the code will not execute at all.

